The reload of new code from the file of a running program
(docs/PROGRAMS.md, "New code in a running program"). The new module
beam_com_reload of kernel watches the path of the file of the program
(-beam_com_exe). When a new file takes its place (zip writes a new file
and renames it), it reads the zip of the new file as a plain file, and
loads each changed module: Cosmopolitan maps /zip one time, at the start,
so /zip keeps the old file. kernel_safe_sup starts it as a temporary
child, only with -beam_com_reload MS of beam.com (c_src/cosmo/beam_com.c).

